---

<section class="hero" id="hero" data-label="home">
  <div class="hero-photo">
    <img src="/profile.jpg" alt="Elvis Ezimako" />
  </div>

  <div class="kicker reveal">// cs student · networking &amp; security</div>
  <h1 class="reveal">
    Computer science student,<br /><span class="dim">going deep on</span> networking
    &amp; security.
  </h1>
  <div class="bio reveal">
    <div class="who">~$ whoami</div>
    <p>
      I started in code, but the moment I understood how data actually moves
      across a network, that was it. Now my time goes to packets, ports, and
      protocols — how connections work, and how to keep them from being abused.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="status reveal">
    <span class="led"></span><span class="mono"
      >studying for CCNA · wiring up my first home lab</span
    >
  </div>
  <div class="cta reveal">
    <a href="#projects" class="btn solid">See my work</a>
    <a
      href="https://github.com/ULTRONLORD"
      class="btn line"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a
    >
  </div>
</section>
<div class="panel-strip reveal" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="p"></span><span class="p on"></span><span class="p"></span><span
    class="p"></span>
  <span class="cbl"></span>
  <span class="p"></span><span class="p"></span><span class="p"></span>
</div>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
  }

  .hero-photo {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
  }

  .hero-photo img {
    width: 160px;
    height: 160px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 3px solid #00f0ff;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 20px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.4),
      0 0 40px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);
    transition: box-shadow 0.3s ease;
  }

  .hero-photo img:hover {
    box-shadow:
      0 0 30px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.6),
      0 0 60px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.25);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero-photo {
      position: static;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
